desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Prefer Write In Binary Mode"
	title_zh: "Prefer Write In Binary Mode"
	type: portability
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-portability-prefer-write-in-binary-mode"
	risk: "code-style"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `prefer-write-in-binary-mode` (ocaml/lang/portability/crlf-support.yaml).
Original message: 'open_out' behaves differently on Windows and on Unix-like systems with respect to line endings. To get the same behavior everywhere, use 'open_out_bin' or 'open_out_gen [Open_binary]'. If you really want LF-to-CRLF translations to take place when running on Windows, use 'open_out_gen [Open_text]'.
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Preferred fix: open_out_bin
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.ml": <<<POS
open_out
POS
	"safefile://pos.ml": <<<NEG
Out_channel.with_open_bin
NEG
)

${*.ml}.pattern_regex(/(?:open_out)/) as $p0
${*.mli}.pattern_regex(/(?:open_out)/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Prefer Write In Binary Mode",
	title_zh: "Prefer Write In Binary Mode",
	message: "Prefer Write In Binary Mode detected.",
}
